  "followNote": "21/10/2026 (Fresco Joomla 1.0.4, ec1c95f833): the pagination's hover, focus and pressed states take the accent fill and its words, as the template fills them with its primary colour: a framework rule on the surface would otherwise outweigh the template's state rule and the link would look the same under the pointer as at rest (HOVER-2). The Joomla contract's dark-band paint rules (HIER-2) have no counterpart here: this contract keeps no band, so the testimonial and ink features headings already take the system's heading colour.",
  "selectors": {
    "display": "h1.wp-block-heading.hero-title",
    "heading": ["main h2.wp-block-heading"],
    "button": [".tracy .wp-block-button__link", ".tracy .wpcf7-submit", ".tracy button.btn"],
    "buttonPrimary": [
      ".tracy .btn-primary > .wp-block-button__link",
      ".tracy a.btn.btn-primary",
      ".tracy button.btn.btn-primary"
    ],
    "card": [".tracy .features-item"]
  },
  "selectorsNote": "Fresco's own markup, as JA Restaurant did (D-34): the base selectors name .tracy-display and .tracy-card, which this theme never prints, so no system reached its display line, section titles, primary button or cards. The body role reads a menu dish's description (p.dish-description), not the 300-weight lead paragraph above it, as on the Joomla release.",
  "ready": true,
  "readyNote": "measured 22/10/2026 (second pass) on the release of 1.0.0 (release folder restored on a stand of its own, release-measure.mjs: flow.mjs with the 15 featured systems, native and derived side, then the preview on 22 pages at light and dark under the two preview systems; design-system-measurement.json of 1.0.0): TDSR 47 PASS, 0 FAIL, 0 must-fix. HIER-2 was the one rule left: the dark ink bands (.acm-hero, .acm-features.style-1, .acm-testimonial) painted their words with one rule over h1-h6 and the paragraphs (colour text-2) and a second over h1-h6 only (colour text); the first names a:not(...) in its list, so its specificity outweighed the second and a band heading took the quiet text-2 where the same headings outside a band took the heading colour (About Restaurant, HOW TO FIND US? under Moxie and Figma, dark). The first rule no longer lists h1-h6, so the second one wins on them. LAYOUT-3 and ICON-1 are answered from this contract (sideRules), LAYOUT-1 from the theme (gd.css): tasks/ja-fresco-wp7/STATUS.md. Release 1.0.1 (database only, same theme) clears the Customize rule PAGE-5: the Go somewhere button of the typography page now points to /contact. Re-measured 22/10/2026 on the release folder of 1.0.1 (design-system-measurement.json of 1.0.1): TDSR 47 PASS, 0 FAIL.",
  "keepScopes": [".acm-hero", ".acm-features", ".acm-testimonial"],
  "bands": {
    ".acm-hero": {
      "ground": "#0a0b0a",
      "texts": ["#cecece", "#ffffff"],
      "kind": "ink",
      "repaint": true,
      "vars": {
        "--jf-bg": "ground",
        "--wp--preset--color--bg": "ground",
        "--jf-heading": "text",
        "--wp--preset--color--fg-2": "text",
        "--jf-text": "text-2",
        "--wp--preset--color--fg": "text-2"
      },
      "important": true,
      "paint": {
        "&": {
          "color": "text"
        },
        ":is(p, li, span, small, strong, em, label, a:not([class*=btn]):not([class*=button]))": {
          "color": "text-2"
        },
        ":is(h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6)": {
          "color": "text"
        }
      }
    },
    ".acm-features.style-1": {
      "ground": "#0a0b0a",
      "texts": ["#ffffff", "#cecece"],
      "kind": "ink",
      "repaint": true,
      "vars": {
        "--jf-bg": "ground",
        "--wp--preset--color--bg": "ground",
        "--jf-heading": "text",
        "--wp--preset--color--fg-2": "text",
        "--jf-text": "text-2",
        "--wp--preset--color--fg": "text-2"
      },
      "important": true,
      "paint": {
        "&": {
          "color": "text"
        },
        ":is(p, li, span, small, strong, em, label, a:not([class*=btn]):not([class*=button]))": {
          "color": "text-2"
        },
        ":is(h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6)": {
          "color": "text"
        }
      }
    },
    ".acm-testimonial": {
      "ground": "#1b1a1c",
      "texts": ["#ffffff"],
      "kind": "ink",
      "repaint": true,
      "vars": {
        "--jf-bg": "ground",
        "--wp--preset--color--bg": "ground",
        "--jf-heading": "text",
        "--wp--preset--color--fg-2": "text",
        "--jf-text": "text-2",
        "--wp--preset--color--fg": "text-2",
        "--jf-surface": "ground",
        "--wp--preset--color--surface": "ground"
      },
      "important": true,
      "paint": {
        "&": {
          "color": "text"
        },
        ":is(p, li, span, small, strong, em, label, a:not([class*=btn]):not([class*=button]))": {
          "color": "text-2"
        },
        ":is(h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6)": {
          "color": "text"
        }
      }
    },
    ".acm-features.style-2": {
      "ground": "#e6c9a2",
      "texts": [],
      "kind": "brand",
      "repaint": true,
      "important": true,
      "vars": {
        "--jf-accent": "ground",
        "--wp--preset--color--accent": "ground",
        "--jf-accent-on": "text",
        "--jf-heading": "text",
        "--wp--preset--color--fg-2": "text",
        "--jf-text": "text",
        "--wp--preset--color--fg": "text",
        "--jf-surface": "card",
        "--wp--preset--color--surface": "card",
        "--jf-bg": "ground",
        "--wp--preset--color--bg": "ground"
      },
      "paint": {
        "&": {
          "color": "text"
        },
        ":is(h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, p, li, span, small, strong, em, label, a:not([class*=btn]):not([class*=button]))": {
          "color": "text"
        },
        ":is(h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6)": {
          "color": "text"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "sideRules": {
    "light": {
      "img.custom-logo": {
        "filter": "invert(1)"
      },
      ".wp-block-button:is(.btn, .btn-primary)": {
        "border-radius": "var(--ds-btn-radius)"
      },
      ".acm-teams.style-1 .member-social .wp-social-link.wp-social-link": {
        "background-color": "var(--ds-c-surface-warm)",
        "color": "var(--ds-c-fg)"
      },
      ".category-name.wp-block-post-terms a": {
        "border-radius": "var(--ds-btn-radius)",
        "border": "1px solid var(--ds-c-border)"
      },
      ".tracy [class*=\"btn-outline-\"]": {
        "background-image": "none"
      },
      ".ja-masthead:has(.wp-block-cover__image-background).wp-block-cover::before": {
        "background": "linear-gradient(rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3) 0%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7) 100%)"
      },
      ".ja-masthead:has(.wp-block-cover__image-background) :is(.ja-masthead-title, .ja-masthead-description, .ja-masthead-description p)": {
        "color": "var(--ds-c-bg)"
      },
      ".ja-masthead.wp-block-cover:not(:has(.wp-block-cover__image-background))": {
        "background-color": "var(--ds-c-bg)"
      },
      ".ja-masthead:not(:has(.wp-block-cover__image-background)) .wp-block-cover__background": {
        "display": "none"
      },
      ".jf-authors .author-socials .wp-social-link.wp-social-link": {
        "background-color": "var(--ds-c-surface-warm)",
        "color": "var(--ds-c-fg)"
      },
      ".bd-example.gap-1:not(.align-items-center)": {
        "column-gap": "0 !important",
        "row-gap": "0.5rem !important"
      }
    },
    "dark": {
      ".wp-block-button:is(.btn, .btn-primary)": {
        "border-radius": "var(--ds-btn-radius)"
      },
      ".category-name.wp-block-post-terms a": {
        "border-radius": "var(--ds-btn-radius)",
        "border": "1px solid var(--ds-c-border)"
      },
      ".tracy [class*=\"btn-outline-\"]": {
        "background-image": "none"
      },
      ".bd-example.gap-1:not(.align-items-center)": {
        "column-gap": "0 !important",
        "row-gap": "0.5rem !important"
      }
    }
  },
  "sideRulesNote": "mirrors joomla-ja-fresco sideRules: under a light system a masthead that has a photo keeps a dark veil and its words take the page colour, and the logo made for the dark page is inverted; a masthead with no photo is a cover whose core black ground showed under a light system (the page-coloured title on black, EMPTY-1/CON-2), so it takes the page colour instead"
}
